Our pre-challenge blurb tells us we are going to learn about how networks actually work: IP addresses, VLANs, firewalls, ports, protocols, and DNS.

Our learning objectives are:
- Learn the basics of networking
- Identify whether an IP address is public or private
- Explain the purpose of network segmentation and VLANs
- Map IP address ranges to network zones
- Recognize common port numbers and their associated services
- Distinguish between TCP and UDP protocols
- Explain how DNS translates domain names to IP addresses
- Trace network activity across DNS, flow, and proxy logs
- Identify indicators of compromise (IOCs) including malicious domains and IPs
- Recognize C2 beaconing patterns in network traffic
- Correlate phishing emails to resulting network compromise

Our tags for this module are: Analyzing Network , Understanding Network Communication, Pivoting Across Data

